1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:24,720
Hey folks, I'm Cori and I work at Positive Approach to Care.

2
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:42,380
I recently was talking to someone who was living with dementia and she was telling me about all the different ways that she sets up some cues and some checks and balances to make sure that she gets to the appointments that she needs to get to and remembers to do the things that she needs to do.

3
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:54,260
With so much going on in our lives between work and leisure time, making sure we get enough rest and restoration, it's easy for things to get mixed in the shuffle.

4
00:00:54,720 --> 00:01:06,340
So what she was telling me is that all of the methods that she's used to get to this point are all based on things that she's always done in her life.

5
00:01:06,340 --> 00:01:09,180
Like post-it notes are a really great example.

6
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:24,040
So today I thought I would spend a little time sharing with you what I do to help me remember things so that you might think about things that would work for you based on what you've always done.

7
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:24,560
Or,

8
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:42,240
if you're supporting someone who's living with dementia, find out more about the things that they've always done to help them get to where they need to be and see how those apply to what you're currently doing to figure out what's helpful and what's not helpful.

9
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:48,240
As you're watching this video, I'd like for you to think about what kind of learner you are.

10
00:01:48,240 --> 00:01:53,640
For me, I'm a kinesthetic learner and part of that means that I am always on the move.

11
00:01:53,640 --> 00:01:54,640
So what works really well is timing things out.

12
00:01:54,640 --> 00:02:01,120
really well for me is to have visual verbal cues placed in different places around the house so

13
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:07,520
that it's easy for me to recognize that something needs to be done. What I'm about to show you are

14
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:14,220
some images of notes that are posted around my house that help me remember to take care of my

15
00:02:14,220 --> 00:02:23,980
business when I'm at home. This first image probably won't come as a surprise to you. It's a list. We

16
00:02:23,980 --> 00:02:29,800
keep this list for our groceries on the counter next to the refrigerator so that anytime we run

17
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:34,900
out of something or we think of something new we want to get, we add it to the list and when it's

18
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:40,660
time to go to the store we know exactly what we need to purchase. Whiteboards are another really

19
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:46,240
handy tool to have around the house. On the left you'll see an image of a whiteboard that I use in

20
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:52,100
my office to keep track of appointments and tasks that I need to take care of in any specific week.

21
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:53,960
The image on the right shows a whiteboard that I use to keep track of my appointments and tasks that I need to take care of in any specific week. The image on the

22
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:59,640
right is a whiteboard calendar that I purchased at a local office supply store.

23
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:03,980
It has an adhesive backing that won't damage your walls and it's great because

24
00:03:03,980 --> 00:03:07,520
we hung it in our stairwell so that every day as we go up and down the

25
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:12,300
stairs we have a visual reminder of things that are coming up. Because this

26
00:03:12,300 --> 00:03:16,840
calendar functions like a whiteboard you do have to go through and wipe it clean

27
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:21,080
every month and then write out your activities for the next month. You can

28
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:23,400
see here that I have spilled the

29
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:23,940
calendar of 10 왼� cover laughs

30
00:03:23,940 --> 00:03:27,400
so that it encompasses part of February and March.

31
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:31,320
But I really like that because I've created a ritual for myself

32
00:03:31,320 --> 00:03:35,260
where I sit down once a month and look at the month as a whole

33
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:39,300
so that I really get the big picture of where our commitments are

34
00:03:39,300 --> 00:03:42,020
and where we need to carve out some time for ourselves.

35
00:03:43,060 --> 00:03:46,540
Then there are other days when you just need a post-it note.

36
00:03:47,140 --> 00:03:51,140
In our house, you'll often find a note stuck right to the door

37
00:03:51,140 --> 00:03:55,920
so that before you leave, you don't forget that really important thing you wanted to remember.

38
00:04:21,140 --> 00:04:39,120
If you're looking for a more long-term solution,

39
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:41,680
you might consider purchasing a label maker.

40
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:49,120
This is a great way to put a more permanent message

41
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:51,120
exactly where you want it to be.

42
00:04:51,140 --> 00:04:51,980
You'll find that you need it.

43
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:59,400
In the examples we've looked at so far,

44
00:04:59,660 --> 00:05:01,240
you've seen a lot of words.

45
00:05:01,720 --> 00:05:04,380
Notice they're also on different types of paper.

46
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:07,900
That's one way that we catch our visual attention

47
00:05:07,900 --> 00:05:11,680
by seeing that paper in a place we don't usually see one.

48
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:15,600
And then we can read the words to get the message.

49
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:18,000
Another option that you have

50
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,900
is to give yourself a more visual cue.

51
00:05:21,140 --> 00:05:25,600
In this example, you see the green bin sitting in the floor

52
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:27,460
right in the middle of the kitchen.

53
00:05:27,460 --> 00:05:31,800
When I see this green bin here, or when I set it out for myself,

54
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:35,460
I know that I'm setting up a reminder to do some maintenance.

55
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:39,300
And everything I need to do the maintenance is in that bin.

56
00:05:39,300 --> 00:05:42,800
Once the project is finished, I put the bin away.

57
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:47,340
You do want to be careful to make sure that you're not creating a trip hazard.

58
00:05:47,340 --> 00:05:49,880
We definitely want to keep everyone safe.

59
00:05:49,880 --> 00:05:53,880
Now for me and my house, we're currently aging normally.

60
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:57,480
But for some folks who may have difficulty reading,

